Test libhugetlbfs with testsuite from the libhugetlbfs source rpm.
This is mainly for testing the libhugetlbfs itself, not for kernel.
So this run the version with the srpm and run for ystream test.

While KT1 test /kernel/vm/hugepage/libhugetlbfs focus on kernel.

This testcase contains two parts:
  - Function Test
  - Stress Test

Parameters
  - TESTARGS        For the total memory for hugepages in kB.
  - TEST_VERSION    For the libhugetlbfs srpm version.  E.G. 2.21-16.el8
  - REPO_URL        For the extra yum repo link, used for installing extra
                    packages in dependency.sh. E.G.
                    http://download.devel.redhat.com/rel-eng/rhel-8/RHEL-8/latest-RHEL-8.1.0/compose/CRB/x86_64/os/
  - DOWNLOAD_LINK   For the libhugetlbfs rpm download base url(default is brew), the download
                    address would be $DOWNLOAD_LINK/$version/$release/$arch/libhugetlbfs.rpm
                    If the absolute path of the rpms are defined with like below, rpms will be downlaoded one by one
                    DOWNLOAD_LINK="http://xxxx/libhugetlbfs.rpm http://xxxxx/libhugetlb.src.rpm"
                    If 'yum' is in the arg, the libhugetlbfs will be downloaded with 'dnf download'.
                    'yum' and direct rpm link can be used together, E.G.
                    DOWNLOAD_LINK="yum http://xxxxx/libhugetlb.src.rpm"
